---
import LegalPageLayout from "../layouts/LegalPageLayout.astro";
import { webappBaseUrl } from "../lib/publicUrls";

const sectionClass = "border-t border-white/35 py-8 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0";
const copyClass = "max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-white/72 sm:text-base sm:leading-8";
---

<LegalPageLayout
  title="Website Terms | Monarchic"
  description="Terms for using the public monarchic.io corporate website, research pages, and published website materials."
  path="/terms"
  eyebrow="Legal / Corporate website"
  heading="Website Terms"
  introduction="These terms apply to the public monarchic.io corporate website and its published materials. Product accounts, billing, hosted MCPs, and agent services use separate terms."
  effectiveDate="August 22, 2026"
  documentId="website-terms"
  contactId="terms-contact"
>
  <a slot="toc" href="#scope" class="hover:text-signal">Scope</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#use" class="hover:text-signal">Site use</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#materials" class="hover:text-signal">Materials</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#research" class="hover:text-signal">Research</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#external" class="hover:text-signal">External links</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#disclaimer" class="hover:text-signal">Disclaimer</a>
  <a slot="toc" href="#changes" class="hover:text-signal">Changes</a>

  <section id="scope" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Scope</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>These terms govern access to the informational pages, product descriptions, research reports, downloadable website materials, and product waitlist on monarchic.io.</p>
      <p>They do not govern account creation, subscriptions, payment, hosted MCP calls, agent runs, customer content, service levels, or product support. Those activities are covered by the <a class="font-bold text-signal hover:text-white" href={`${webappBaseUrl}/terms`}>Monarchic product terms</a> and any applicable order or agreement.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="use" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Permitted site use</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>You may browse the site, evaluate public product information, read published research, link to public pages, and use downloadable materials under the license stated with those materials.</p>
      <p>Do not interfere with site operation, probe or bypass security controls, distribute malware, misrepresent affiliation with Monarchic, use the site to violate law or third-party rights, or impose an unreasonable automated load. Authorized security research should follow the process on the <a class="font-bold text-signal hover:text-white" href="/security">security page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="materials" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Website materials and names</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>Monarchic retains rights in its website design, original copy, product names, trademarks, and materials unless a page or linked repository states another license. Access to the website does not grant a trademark license or a right to imply endorsement.</p>
      <p>Open-source code, datasets, papers, benchmark artifacts, and third-party materials remain subject to their own notices and licenses. Check the linked source before reuse.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="research" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Research and product information</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>Research results apply to the named dataset, method, version, metric, and artifact. A benchmark does not establish general product performance, comparative superiority, production latency, or suitability for a specific use unless the report states that scope.</p>
      <p>Product availability, lifecycle labels, pricing, and feature descriptions may change. A Coming soon or In rollout label does not promise a launch date. Verify current product status and the terms presented in the webapp before relying on a purchase or deployment decision.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="external" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">External links and product applications</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>The site links to source repositories, research projects, service providers, and the Monarchic webapp. External destinations control their own content, availability, security, and terms.</p>
      <p>A link is provided for context or access and does not by itself endorse every claim, product, or practice at the destination.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="disclaimer" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Informational boundary</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>The corporate website is provided for general information and product evaluation. Content may contain errors, become outdated, or omit facts relevant to your situation. Use primary artifacts and professional review for consequential technical, scientific, legal, financial, or business decisions.</p>
      <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, Monarchic does not promise uninterrupted website availability or that every public page will always be complete, current, or error-free. Product commitments arise only from the applicable product terms, checkout statement, order, or signed agreement.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" class={sectionClass}>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Changes and contact</h2>
    <div class={copyClass}>
      <p>We may update the website and these terms as the company, products, or publication practices change. The effective date identifies the current website-terms version.</p>
      <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to <a class="font-bold text-signal hover:text-white" href="mailto:support@monarchic.io?subject=Website%20terms">support@monarchic.io</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div slot="contact">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase text-signal">Website terms</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase">Questions about public website use?</h2>
  </div>
  <div slot="contact" class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a href="mailto:support@monarchic.io?subject=Website%20terms" class="border-2 border-signal bg-signal px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase text-black transition hover:bg-signal-soft">Contact support</a>
    <a href={`${webappBaseUrl}/terms`} class="border-2 border-white/50 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase text-white transition hover:border-signal hover:bg-signal/10 hover:text-signal-soft">Product terms</a>
  </div>
</LegalPageLayout>
